   "source": "# Benchmark Model 2 — POSTER++ (Literature Benchmark)\n**EmpathBot · CS731 Group 14 | Preeti · TJ · Kanishka**\n\n---\n\n### What this notebook does\nDownloads the **published POSTER++ pre-trained weights** and evaluates them on the standard  \nRAF-DB 7-class test set (3,068 images). No training from scratch — we reproduce the  \npublished **92.21% accuracy** figure to establish our literature benchmark.\n\nThis is the number we compare *all* of our models against. If EmpathBot's model  \ncomes within 3–5% of POSTER++ on our 6-class task, we have a defensible result.\n\n### Why POSTER++ is the right benchmark\n- Published in *IEEE TPAMI 2023* (Mao et al.) — peer-reviewed, reproducible\n- State-of-the-art on RAF-DB as of this project's literature review\n- Architecture is publicly released with pre-trained weights\n- Represents what \"best available FER model\" looks like today\n\n### What we expect\n- Reproduced accuracy should be ≈92.21% (within ±0.5% due to hardware/seed differences)\n- If it differs by >2%, the wrong checkpoint or wrong RAF-DB split is being used\n\n### Inputs\n| File / folder | What it is |\n|---|---|\n| `data/RAF-DB/basic/Image/aligned/` | RAF-DB pre-aligned face images |\n| `data/RAF-DB/basic/EmoLabel/list_patition_label.txt` | Train/test labels (1–7, 1-indexed) |\n| `POSTER_V2/` | Cloned POSTER++ repo (auto-created in Cell 4) |\n| `models/posterv2_rafdb.pth` | Downloaded pre-trained checkpoint (~1.5 GB) |\n\n### Outputs\n| File | What it is |\n|---|---|\n| `results/posterv2_results.json` | Test accuracy, F1, per-class metrics |\n| `results/posterv2_confusion_matrix.png` | Confusion matrix plot |\n| `results/posterv2_benchmark_comparison.png` | Bar chart vs published 92.21% |"
