   "source": "---\n## Cell 3 — What is POSTER++?\n\n**POSTER++** (Pyramid crOSS-fusionTransformER v2, Mao et al., *IEEE TPAMI 2023*) is the  \nstate-of-the-art FER model used as this project's literature benchmark.\n\n**Architecture in plain English:**\n1. A **ResNet-50** backbone extracts rich global face features\n2. A **ViT-B/16** image encoder adds transformer-level multi-scale understanding\n3. A second **ViT** landmark encoder explicitly encodes 68 facial keypoints (eyes, nose, lips)\n4. A **Pyramid Cross-Fusion Transformer** combines landmark and image features at multiple scales\n\nThis pyramid design makes POSTER++ robust to pose variation and partial occlusion — the two  \nbiggest failure modes of simpler CNN-based FER models like our ResNet-18 baseline.\n\n**Why 92.21% is hard to beat:**\n- Trained on 12,271 RAF-DB training images with heavy augmentation\n- Uses both appearance (pixels) and geometry (landmarks) simultaneously\n- Fine-tuned specifically for FER with a curated pre-training regime\n- The gap between 92.21% and human performance (~95%) is very small\n\nFor EmpathBot, we don't need to beat POSTER++. We need to show we understand the landscape  \nand that our model choice is reasonable for our 6-class emotion task."
  },
